// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_direct_8a.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: the $8A direct-construction clause added to raster_program's tree-wide
//          scan (spec §4.2b precedent: constructor-only refusals are not refusals —
//          Task 8 review, review finding I-3).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "detonates the relative-arm chain"
//
// THE DODGE, spelled out — same shape as poison_direct_8f.emp, different register.
// `RasterOp.SetReg($8A05)` is the enum variant reg_set returns, constructed by
// hand — so reg_set's own $0A ensure never runs and the write reaches the encoder
// with nothing having looked at it. The enum is `pub` (it has to be: the encoder's
// match arms are the public wire contract), so this is not a hypothetical spelling,
// it is one the language admits today.
//
// Reg $0A is the raster SCHEDULE's own register: Raster_HInt writes the record's
// arm word to reg $0A FIRST and only then runs the record's ops
// (engine/effects/raster.emp, Raster_HInt: `move.w (a1)+, (a2)` before `.op_loop`).
// A `$8Axx` op in the record's own op list overwrites the arm the encoder just
// scheduled, so the counter reloads with the author's value at the next HInt and
// every remaining fire in the frame lands on the wrong line — detonating the
// relative-arm chain from that fire down, silently.
//
// That is why the refusal is TWO layers here too. reg_set's constructor ensure is
// the one that gives an author a good sentence at the call site; this scan is the
// one that cannot be dodged, running on every program in the tree whether or not
// it has a band.
//
// NO IMPORTS — see poison_four_bands.emp's note.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_direct_8a

const POISON_DIRECT_8A = [
    fire(100, [RasterOp.SetReg($8A05)]),
]

ensure(raster_program(POISON_DIRECT_8A).len > 0,
       "poison_direct_8a: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
